.archon-horizon/runs/0202/sessions/0004-horizon-ajcr-complete/transcript.jsonl:223:{"kind": "tool_result", "at": "2026-09-01T16:01:09.595000+00:00", "text": "", "tool": "", "data": {"content": [{"type": "input_text", "text": "Script completed\nWall time 0.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"}, {"type": "input_text", "text": "=== r0198 ===\n## Progress\n\n- Replaced unstable inferred tensor/ring/algebra witnesses with pinned restriction maps, named pullback legs, and public projection laws.\n- Refactored Diagram, PreSnd, Snd, and GluedComparison proofs to use localized owner-side equalities. The Diagram artifact shrank from 536,952 to 424,792 bytes.\n- Exported pinned chart finite-presentation/type witnesses and audited them through `Pic0CriticalPath`.\n- All targeted checks passed; `Pic0CriticalPath` passed in 16.7s and the full `AlgebraicJacobian` umbrella passed in 14.7s. No new `sorry` or `admit`.\n- Final code commits include `15d71a94c1` and `5d9073c2ee`. Roadmap/task state is committed in `a5c013368e`; final inbox handoff state is committed in `f905d0f679`.\n- The task and complete base-change roadmap cone are marked done.\n\n## Issues\n\n- Diagram serialization remains expensive at roughly 865.8s, including 477s serialization.\n- Stronger symmetric API experiments regressed and remain preserved as rejected attempts `0003` and `0004`.\n- Historical run-0198 report placeholders are tracked for tooling follow-up in `I-2216`.\n\n## Why I stopped\n\nThe API-redesign objective is fully complete, root-verified, and committed. Remaining representability and orbit-affineness obligations are separate mathematical gaps.\n\n## Next\n\nProceed with the exact-carrier representability and orbit-affineness arguments using the stabilized finite-stage API.\n"}, {"type": "input_text", "text": "=== r0194s8 ===\n## Progress\n\n- [Pic0FiniteStageFinalBaseChange.lean:938](/home/axel/LeanAlgebraicGeometry-Horizon/MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild/AlgebraicJacobian/Picard/Pic0Finite