pped\n\nThe objective is partly advanced. The main unstable finite-stage boundaries now expose verified witness-bearing APIs, but DiagramIso migration, final-base-change naturality, producer migration, and representability endpoints remain open.\n\n## Next\n\nBuild `Pic0FiniteStageRestrictionNaturality` in isolation, then verify and commit the DiagramIso direct import and presentation adapter. Continue migrating legacy GlueData consumers through `P.presentation`, then address final naturality and producer obligations.\n\nReport: [report.md](/home/axel/LeanAlgebraicGeometry-Horizon/.archon-horizon/runs/0194/sessions/0004-horizon-ajcr-finite-stage-api-redesign/report.md)\n"}, {"type": "input_text", "text": "=== r0198ground ===\n**Findings**\n\n1. **High: the consumer cone is still uncertified.** `GluingDiagramIso`, top `PreSnd`, and `Snd` now have fresh passing builds and `.olean` files. The next check, [Pic0FiniteStageGluedComparison.lean](/home/axel/LeanAlgebraicGeometry-Horizon/MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild/AlgebraicJacobian/Picard/Pic0FiniteStageGluedComparison.lean:270), failed after 375s at the inverse-law proof with deterministic `whnf`/`isDefEq` heartbeat exhaustion; `gluingGluedIso` being unknown was cascading. No `GluedComparison.olean` exists, and [Pic0CriticalPath.lean](/home/axel/LeanAlgebraicGeometry-Horizon/MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild/AlgebraicJacobian/Picard/Pic0CriticalPath.lean:1) still imports neither `Snd` nor `GluedComparison`. The new unstaged split into `gluingGluedHom_inv`/`gluingGluedInv_hom` directly targets the failure but is not yet accepted evidence.\n\n2. **High: roadmap and graph state lag the actual frontier.** `compile-diagram-iso`, `diagram-left-leg`, `pre-snd`, and `snd` remain `blocked` although their final recorded module builds pass. `compile-glue-package` is `done` while containing that blocked descendant chain, producing Horizon’s parent/child warning. Reparent the “separate” diagram cha