 (tangentTestObject R) x :=\n  rfl\n\nomit [CommRing R] in\ntheorem tangentMap_id {F : Type u → Type v} :\n    tangentMap R (F := F) (G := F) (fun _ x => x) =\n      (id : tangentSpace R F → tangentSpace R F) := by\n  rfl\n\nomit [CommRing R] in\ntheorem tangentMap_comp {F G H : Type u → Type v}\n    (η : ∀ A : Type u, F A → G A) (θ : ∀ A : Type u, G A → H A) :\n    tangentMap R (F := F) (G := H) (fun A x => θ A (η A x)) =\n      (tangentMap R θ) ∘ (tangentMap R η) := by\n  rfl\n\nend\n\nend StacksPart06Lib\n", "exit_code": 0}, "usage": null}
748:{"kind": "tool_result", "at": "2026-08-27T15:10:32.924000+00:00", "text": "", "tool": "", "data": {"content": [{"type": "input_text", "text": "Script completed\nWall time 8.9 seconds\nOutput:\n"}, {"type": "input_text", "text": "---hgraph/nodes/50323f473890.md\n---\nauthor: sync\nchapter: Formal Deformation Theory\ncontent_type: definition\ncreated: '2026-08-27T16:30:40'\ngenerated: blueprint\ngroup: formal-defos\nlabel: formal-defos-definition-tangent-space\nlean_status: empty\norder: 81\nref: stacks:06IG\ntitle: Tangent space\ntype: tex\nupdated: '2026-08-27T16:30:40'\n---\n\\href{https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/06IG}{\\texttt{Stacks tag 06IG}}\n\n\nLet $\\mathcal{F}$ be a predeformation category.\nThe {\\it tangent space $T \\mathcal{F}$ of $\\mathcal{F}$}\nis the set $\\overline{\\mathcal{F}}(k[\\epsilon])$\nof isomorphism classes of objects in the fiber category $\\mathcal\nF(k[\\epsilon])$.---hgraph/nodes/5a2d18addba9.md\n---\nauthor: sync\nchapter: Formal Deformation Theory\ncontent_type: lemma\ncreated: '2026-08-27T16:30:40'\ngenerated: blueprint\ngroup: formal-defos\nlabel: formal-defos-lemma-preserves-products\nlean_status: empty\norder: 72\nref: stacks:06I9\ntitle: Preserves products\ntype: tex\nupdated: '2026-08-27T16:30:40'\n---\n\\href{https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/06I9}{\\texttt{Stacks tag 06I9}}\n\n\nLet $R$ be an $S$-algebra. Then the functor\n$\\text{Mod}_R \\to S\\text{-Alg}/R$ described above preserves finite products.---hgraph/nodes/a9d0b9dec877.md\n---\nauthor: sync\nchapter: Formal Deformation Theory\ncontent_type: definition\ncreated: '2026-08-27T16:30:40'\ngenerated: blueprint\ngroup: formal-defos\nlabel: formal-defos-definition-tangent-space-over-R\nlean_status: empty\norder: 74\nref: stacks:06IB\ntitle: Tangent space over R\ntype: tex\nupdated: '2026-08-27T16:30:40'\n---\n\\href{https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/06IB}{\\texttt{Stacks tag 06IB}}\n\n\nLet $\\mathcal{C}$ be a category as in\nLemma \\ref{formal-defos-lemma-tangent-space-functor}.\nLet $F : \\mathcal{C} \\to \\textit{Sets}$ be a functor such that\n$F(R)$ is a one element set. The {\\it tangent space $TF$ of $F$} is\n$F(R[\\epsilon])$.---hgraph/nodes/c1ec2b9dc01a.md\n---\nauthor: sync\nchapter: Formal Deformation Theory\ncontent_type: lemma\ncreated: '2026-08-27T16:30:40'\ngenerated: blueprint\ngroup: formal-defos\nlabel: formal-defos-lemma-tangent-space-functor\nlean_status: empty\norder: 73\nref: stacks:06IA\ntitle: Tangent space functor\ntype: tex\nupdated: '2026-08-27T16:30:40'\n---\n\\href{https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/06IA}{\\texttt{Stacks tag 06IA}}\n\n\nLet $R$ be an $S$-algebra, and let $\\mathcal{C}$ be a strictly full\nsubcategory of $S\\text{-Alg}/R$ containing $R[M]$ for all\n$M \\in \\Ob(\\text{Mod}^{fg}_R)$.\nLet $F: \\mathcal{C} \\to \\textit{Sets}$ be a functor. Suppose that\n$F(R)$ is a one element set and that for any $M, N \\in\n\\Ob(\\text{Mod}^{fg}_R)$, the induced map\n$$\nF(R[M] \\times_R R[N]) \\to F(R[M]) \\times F(R[N])\n$$\nis a bijection. Then $F(R[M])$ has a natural $R$-module structure for any $M\n\\in \\Ob(\\text{Mod}^{fg}_R)$.---GRAPH STATS---\n[HORIZON] ◈ REQUIRED · 3 active protections: I-0074 \"**FGA picSharp rewire \nLANDED (run 0008): rout...\"; I-2034 \" FS blueprints frozen except corr...\"; \nI-2035 \" FS cross-project read, single-pr...\" — consult before editing: `horizon\ninbox list --mine --status open --kind protection --json`\n[HORIZON] ◈ Advisory · 17 unread inbox items: I-1664 \"A LOCALISATION REDUCTION \nIS EMPTIED BY THE CO...\"; I-1979 \"AJCR lake stale-trace and scheduling race \nyie...\"; I-2039 \"Workspace baseline/integration commits repeat...\"; +14 more — \nreview when relevant: `horizon inbox list --mine --unread --json`\n[HORIZON] ◈ session running 1h41m, 2.0k tokens out\n[HORIZON] ◈ Running sessions: run 0163 · task ajcr-finite-stage-api-redesign; \nrun 0179 · task fs-milne; run 0180 · task fs-mumford; run 0181 · task \nfs-hartshorne — message a team wit